### Session 4 IPL: orchestrating Book and BookCopy.
### In the seed data only two copies have Status 'D' (available):
###   0099826704 copy 1 (The Firm) and 0099895102 copy 1 (Jurassic Park).
### Every other seeded copy has a NULL Status, so it is NOT available.

### Rent an available copy (200). The Controller checks first, then writes.
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/rent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 1 }

### Rent the same copy again: the check fails, nothing is written (409)
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/rent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 1 }

### A copy that does not exist: valid on its own, not a real row (404)
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/rent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 9 }

### Bad copyNo: one Joi schema checks both fields together (400)
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/rent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 0 }

### Short isbn (400)
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/rent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "123", "copyNo": 1 }

### Delete a copy, now wrapped in try / catch (204, then 404 the second time)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/books/0064410935/copies/9

### ---- Practice solution (this branch only): return a copy ----

### Return the copy rented above (200)
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/return
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 1 }

### Return it again: it is not rented (409)
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/return
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 1 }
